<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24386" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δήμιος</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάμ-</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον
			</span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			A.
			<u>Ch.</u>
			57
		</span></i> (lyr.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δημίην: πόρνην</span> (<i><span class="en">
			Cypr.
		</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
			Hsch.
		</span></i>): (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῆμος</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>belonging to the people,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶκος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					20.264
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰσυμνῆται δ.</span> judges
				<i>elected by the people,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				8.259
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρῆξις δ᾽ ἥδ᾽ ἰδίη, οὐ
			δήμιος</span> not <i>public,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				3.82
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δήμιον ἦ ἴδιον;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					4.314
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				2.32
			</span></i>: epith. of Hestia at Paros, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(5).238
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(v B. C.)</span>: neut. pl. as Adv., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δήμια πίνειϝ</span>”
				<i>at the public cost,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.17.250
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ δ.</span>”
				<i>the sovereign people,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					370
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				699
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ δ.</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοῦλος</span>) <i>public executioner,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ec.</u>
				81
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				439e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				13.56
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				2.126
			</span></i>, etc. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάμιος μαστίκτωρ</span> in
				<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				160
			</span></i> (lyr.)); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ κοινὸς δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					872b
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>public physician,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτωχὸς ἦν καζ δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phoenicid.
					4.13
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δημίαι πύλαι,</span> perh. a mistake for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διομῇσι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>